1. Independent implementation, no upstream code

   Every .java file under src/ was written for this project. No source file
   from the Apache Software Foundation or from QOS.ch is included, copied,
   adapted, or redistributed here. This project ships no third-party logging
   jar: LibHome contains only the script engine, the H2 JDBC driver, the
   bundled JDK/Ant, and the JsPlus jars.

   In particular, the Log4j 2 Logger interface and its implementation class
   are generated by build/tools/genLog4j2.py from build/iface-audit/
   log4j2_Logger_official.txt, which is a javap signature dump: it carries
   method names, parameter types, return types and modifiers only - no
   method bodies, no comments, and no parameter names (javap does not emit
   them). Only the API surface is reproduced, so that existing binaries keep
   linking; every method body routes into the JsPlus engine.

