3. Coexistence warning

   These replacement classes declare the same packages as the official
   artifacts. Do NOT put an official logging jar (slf4j-api, commons-logging,
   juli, log4j-1.2, log4j-api) on the same class path, and do not place this
   jar on the module path together with those jars: the packages would split
   (and, under JPMS, collide). Remove the official jar first - that is the
   whole point of this layer.

4. Compatibility is behavioural, not a warranty

   The replacement aims to reproduce the observable behaviour of the official
   APIs (level gating, marker rendering, placeholder expansion, throwable
   handling, and the numeric values of Level/Priority). It does not
   reproduce upstream internals such as appenders, layouts, configuration
   parsing or the Log4j 2 plugin system; calls that touch those areas are
   accepted and turned into no-ops or engine routing, as documented in
   README.md. Behavioural differences are described per family in that file.
